      "title": "7.5.1 Initial concentration method",
      "language": "en",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "b07b1f6c-f5a4-509d-ae86-73be5bffb0d4",
          "pdf_from": 158,
          "pdf_to": 159,
          "note": "Topic 7.5.1, printed pages 158-159 (Table 7.2), as printed."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "In the presence of hydrogen ions, hydrogen peroxide, H₂O₂, reacts with iodide ions to form water and iodine:"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{H2O2_{(aq)} + 2I^-_{(aq)} + 2H^+_{(aq)} -> 2H2O_{(l)} + I2_{(aq)}}",
            "text_alt": "H₂O₂(aq) + 2I⁻(aq) + 2H⁺(aq) → 2H₂O(l) + I₂(aq)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The rate equation for this reaction is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{rate of reaction} = \\frac{k[\\ce{H2O2}]}{[\\ce{I-}]}",
            "text_alt": "rate of reaction = k[H₂O₂] / [I⁻]",
            "book_errors": [
              "k[H₂O₂] / [I⁻]",
              "\\frac{k[\\ce{H2O2}]}{[\\ce{I-}]}"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "correction",
            "title": "Book correction",
            "text": "The rate equation is rate of reaction = k[H₂O₂][I⁻], first order in H₂O₂ and in I⁻; the print divides by [I⁻] instead of multiplying (only the product fits Table 7.2 and the unit dm³ mol⁻¹ s⁻¹)."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The progress of the reaction can be followed by measuring the initial rate of formation of iodine. Table 7.2 shows the rates of reaction obtained using various initial concentrations of each reactant."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The procedure for calculating k is shown below, using the data for experiment 1."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Step 1 Write out the rate equation."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{rate of reaction} = \\frac{k[\\ce{H2O2}]}{[\\ce{I-}]}",
            "text_alt": "rate of reaction = k[H₂O₂] / [I⁻]",
            "book_errors": [
              "k[H₂O₂] / [I⁻]",
              "\\frac{k[\\ce{H2O2}]}{[\\ce{I-}]}"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Step 2 Rearrange the equation in terms of k"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "k = \\frac{\\text{rate} \\times [\\ce{I-}]}{[\\ce{H2O2}]}",
            "text_alt": "k = rate × [I⁻] / [H₂O₂]",
            "book_errors": [
              "rate × [I⁻] / [H₂O₂]",
              "\\frac{\\text{rate} \\times [\\ce{I-}]}{[\\ce{H2O2}]}"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Step 3 Substitute the values"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "k = \\frac{3.50 \\times 10^{-6} \\times (0.0100)}{(0.0200)}",
            "text_alt": "k = 3.50 × 10⁻⁶ × (0.0100) / (0.0200)",
            "book_errors": [
              "3.50 × 10⁻⁶ × (0.0100) / (0.0200)",
              "\\frac{3.50 \\times 10^{-6} \\times (0.0100)}{(0.0200)}"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "k = 1.75 \\times 10^{-2}\\ \\text{dm}^{3}\\,\\text{mol}^{-1}\\,\\text{s}^{-1}",
            "text_alt": "k = 1.75 × 10⁻² dm³ mol⁻¹ s⁻¹"
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "correction",
            "title": "Book correction",
            "text": "Steps 1 to 3 carry the printed fraction. With rate = k[H₂O₂][I⁻], k = rate / ([H₂O₂][I⁻]) = 3.50 × 10⁻⁶ / (0.0200 × 0.0100) = 1.75 × 10⁻² dm³ mol⁻¹ s⁻¹, the book's answer; the printed working 3.50 × 10⁻⁶ × 0.0100 / 0.0200 would give 1.75 × 10⁻⁶."
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "Table 7.2: Effect of change in concentrations of reactants on the rate of reaction",
            "header": [
              "Experiment",
              "[H₂O₂]/ mol dm⁻³",
              "[I⁻]/ mol dm⁻³",
              "[H⁺]/ mol dm⁻³",
              "Initial rate of reaction/ mol dm⁻³ s⁻¹"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "1",
                "0.0200",
                "0.0100",
                "0.0100",
                "3.5 × 10⁻⁶"
              ],
              [
                "2",
                "0.0300",
                "0.0100",
                "0.0100",
                "5.3 × 10⁻⁶"
              ],
              [
                "3",
                "0.0050",
                "0.0200",
                "0.0200",
                "1.75 × 10⁻⁶"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The concentration of hydrogen ions is ignored because [H⁺] does not appear in the rate equation. The reaction is zero order with respect to [H⁺]."
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
